1. Introduction

This report explores two career roles available in Darwin, Northern Territory: Report Writer and Business Analyst.

The purpose of this research is to understand the responsibilities, skills, software tools and learning resources required for both roles. Current job advertisements and online career resources were reviewed to identify common employer expectations.

The findings were then used to create a three-week learning plan.



2. Primary Role – Report Writer

A Report Writer collects, organises and presents information in a clear and professional format.

Reports may be prepared for managers, clients, project teams or other stakeholders.

Main Responsibilities

| Responsibility       | Description                                                           |
| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Research information | Collect relevant information from documents, systems and stakeholders |
| Prepare reports      | Write business, technical and project reports                         |
| Review data          | Analyse information and identify important findings                   |
| Organise content     | Structure reports using headings, sections and summaries              |
| Edit documents       | Check grammar, spelling, formatting and consistency                   |
| Present findings     | Communicate information clearly to the intended audience              |
| Meet deadlines       | Complete reports within the required timeframe                        |



 3. Secondary Role – Business Analyst

A Business Analyst identifies business problems and helps organisations improve their systems, services and processes.

The role involves working with stakeholders, analysing business needs and preparing documentation for project teams.

Main Responsibilities

| Responsibility          | Description                                           |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| Gather requirements     | Identify stakeholder needs and expectations           |
| Analyse processes       | Review current business workflows                     |
| Identify problems       | Find areas that require improvement                   |
| Prepare documentation   | Record business and system requirements               |
| Create process diagrams | Develop visual representations of workflows           |
| Support project teams   | Work with managers, developers and testers            |
| Review solutions        | Check whether completed solutions meet business needs |



 4. Comparison of Roles

| Report Writer                              | Business Analyst                                    |
| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |
| Focuses on producing professional reports  | Focuses on analysing business problems              |
| Organises research, information and data   | Reviews systems, processes and requirements         |
| Requires strong writing and editing skills | Requires strong analytical and communication skills |
| Produces reports, summaries and findings   | Produces requirements and process documents         |
| Commonly uses Word, Excel and PowerPoint   | Commonly uses Jira, Confluence, Visio and SQL       |
| Presents information clearly               | Recommends business improvements                    |

Both roles require strong communication, research, documentation, organisation and time-management skills.



